<BaseLayout
  title="About this site | Masahiro Sadamura"
  description="Operating policy, privacy policy, copyright, and disclaimer for sadamura.jp."
>
  <h1>About this site</h1>

  <p>
    This site (<a href="/en/">https://sadamura.jp/en/</a>) is a personal academic
    site operated by Masahiro Sadamura (<span lang="ja">貞村 真宏 / さだむら まさひろ</span>) as a
    public-facing channel for his research. It is not an institutional site.
  </p>

  <h2>Operating policy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Content reflects the individual views of the researcher and does not represent the official position of any affiliated institution (The University of Osaka Graduate School of Human Sciences and others).</li>
    <li>The most up-to-date publication list is also available on <a href="https://researchmap.jp/sadamuramasahiro?lang=en" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">researchmap</a> and <a href="https://orcid.org/0009-0008-2248-4583" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">ORCID</a>.</li>
    <li>This site offers <a href="/en/services">paid research and academic support</a> (research memos, AI citation audits, graduate admissions coaching, and boarding-school admissions strategy). These are <strong>provided as a sole proprietorship, not as work of any affiliated institution</strong>; the statutory terms of trade are set out in the <a href="/legal" hreflang="ja">legal disclosures (Japanese)</a>.</li>
    <li>Target update cadence: publications within 2 weeks of acceptance/publication; profile within the calendar month of any role change; contact details immediately.</li>
    <li><code>sadamura.com</code> is not operated by Masahiro Sadamura. The only domain he operates is <code>sadamura.jp</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy policy</h2>
  <h3>What we collect</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Analytics</strong>: since October 2026 this site uses <a href="https://marketingplatform.google.com/about/analytics/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics 4</a> (Google LLC, United States).
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Items collected</strong>: the URL and title of the pages you view and when you view them, the referrer (linking site or search engine), browser, operating system, device category and screen size (user agent), approximate location (country and city) and language, page scrolling, and clicks on links to files such as PDFs and to external sites. No personally identifying information such as names or email addresses is collected or sent.</li>
        <li><strong>Cookies</strong>: Google Analytics cookies (<code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code>, valid for up to two years) are stored on your device to tell repeat visits from the same browser apart.</li>
        <li><strong>Recipient and settings</strong>: the data are sent to Google LLC and processed as described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>. Advertising features (Google signals) are turned off and user-level data retention is set to 14 months. Google Analytics 4 does not store IP addresses.</li>
        <li><strong>Purpose</strong>: only to learn which pages and documents are read and to improve the site, in aggregate form that is not linked to any individual.</li>
        <li><strong>Opting out</strong>: block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li><strong>Outbound requests</strong>: web fonts and analytics are provided by Google LLC (United States), so loading a page sends your IP address and related request headers there. No personally identifying information is collected by this site, but compliance with GDPR and CCPA is not warranted unconditionally.</li>
    <li><strong>Direct contact</strong>: only what you put in your message. Received and read by the site owner (technical access by the mail provider aside) and never shared with third parties.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Use</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Collected information is used only to improve the site and to respond to inquiries.</li>
    <li>Information submitted with an order for a <a href="/en/services">paid service</a> is also used to quote, contract, and deliver the service, to issue invoices, and to keep the books and records required by law, as set out in the <a href="/legal" hreflang="ja">legal disclosures (Japanese)</a>.</li>
    <li>Information is never shared with third parties without consent.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Right to erasure</h3>
  <p>To request deletion of any information about yourself, please email the address listed on the <a href="/en/contact">contact page</a>.</p>

  <h2>Copyright and licensing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Text and code on this site are released under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/" rel="license noopener" target="_blank">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a> (non-commercial use only; redistribution requires the same license).</li>
    <li>Published paper PDFs are hosted only when the publisher's license permits self-hosting.</li>
    <li>Research data are released through <a href="https://osf.io/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">OSF</a> and similar repositories under preregistered terms.</li>
    <li>Third-party images, figures, and text are cited and used in accordance with their respective licenses.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    Information on this site reflects the individual views of the researcher and does not represent the official position of any affiliated institution. If you need legal advice, please consult a qualified attorney. The content here is for academic discussion only and does not constitute legal advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Build stack</h2>
  <p>
    This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Astro</a>. The design and information architecture take their cue from Tomoya Mukai's researcher site (<a href="https://mukait.fool.jp/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">mukait.fool.jp</a>).
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>For inquiries about research, collaboration, citations, media requests, or this site, see the <a href="/en/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
